From 2d0067848b1cca51d5ed430453811c214b47d296 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lonkwitz <mawelo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:54:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [AI generated] AIX 7.1/6.1 targets: sysroot tooling,
 static libc++ 19 build, LLVM patches, compat headers

Binaries built with IBM Open XL on AIX 7.2 do not run on 7.1 or 6.1: the IBM
libc++ runtime imports strftime_l (missing in the 7.1 libc) and the 7.2
PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER layout differs from 7.1 (pthread_mutex_lock returns
EINVAL, libc++abi reports "__cxa_guard_acquire failed to acquire mutex").

tools/aix/sysroot71/ builds a sysroot from an installation of the target
release and a static libc++/libc++abi/libunwind (LLVM 19.1.7) against it:

* make_sysroot.pl: unpack, make symlinks relative, use the 7.2 crti_64.o (the
  older one needs libC symbols), guard the C++ overloads in math.h with
  __LIBC_NO_CPP_MATH_OVERLOADS__ as 7.2 does.
* make_cxxwrap.pl: extern "C" wrappers for the C headers of 7.1/6.1, which
  have no such brackets (isdigit, catopen, socket would get C++ linkage).
* build_rt.pl: libunwind, libc++abi, libc++ with the LLVM AIX cache, static,
  with LIBCXXABI_HAS_CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL=OFF.
* llvm-19.1.7-aix-cmake-quote.patch: unquoted ${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} in the
  runtimes' CMake files compares against the CMake variable AIX (value 1) on
  AIX itself, so Unwind_AIXExtras.cpp was not compiled.
* llvm-19.1.7-aix-cxa-thread-atexit.patch: libc++abi references
  __cxa_thread_atexit_impl weakly; XCOFF has no weak undefined symbols and the
  7.1 libc lacks the function.
* aix71_compat.h: strftime_l as static inline (uselocale + strftime),
  noreturn for abort/exit/_Exit (the 7.1 stdlib.h lacks it).
* aix61_compat.h: AIX 6.1 has no POSIX 2008 locale API (locale_t, newlocale,
  uselocale, freelocale, *_l): a single-global-locale shim; O_CLOEXEC. With
  -fno-builtin-strlen -fno-builtin-strcmp (Open XL otherwise references
  ___strlen64/___strcmp64, not exported by the 6.1 libc) and
  -DREMOVE_ALL_USE_DIRECTORY_ITERATOR for libc++ (no openat family on 6.1).

The resulting btop binaries import only libc, libpthreads and libperfstat.
